WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.030
A useful integration technique recognizes the structure that differentiation would create

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:15.133
Here the outside is a power, the inside is x squared plus two, and the nearby factor two x is exactly the inside's derivative.

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:18.020
Name the inside u

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:26.348
The entire combination two x times d x becomes d u, so the integral becomes u cubed with respect to u

00:00:26.348 --> 00:00:31.900
This substitution reverses the chain rule; it does not simply delete an inconvenient factor.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:39.124
Integrating u cubed gives u to the fourth divided by four, plus a constant

00:00:39.124 --> 00:00:42.509
Substitute the original inside back into the answer

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:48.433
Differentiating this result recreates both the outer cube and the required factor two x.

00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:55.009
Products may call for integration by parts, the reverse of the product rule

00:00:55.009 --> 00:01:00.691
Choose u equal to x and d v equal to exponential x d x

00:01:00.691 --> 00:01:05.967
Subtracting the remaining exponential integral gives an answer you can verify by differentiating.
